-- =====================
-- Schema Template: Replace {{KEYSPACE}} with regional keyspace (nam, eur, ocn, eas, sam, sas, gdpr)
-- Applied by ScyllaMigrationService at startup, after 005_marker_color_fixup.
--
-- Narrows users.primary_front from int to smallint (step 1 of 2, paired with 007):
--
--   Every other alter-id column in the schema is smallint (alters.id, tags.alter_id,
--   alter_journals.alter_id, current_fronts.alter_id, fronts.alter_id, ...). The single
--   outlier was users.primary_front, which was created as int back when AlterId's C#
--   backing was also int. Now that AlterId.Value is a short, the int column is a
--   type-mismatch and would force every reader to widen back to int just to talk to it.
--
-- Cassandra / ScyllaDB does not support in-place column-type changes (no
-- `ALTER TABLE MODIFY COLUMN` with a different data type). Migration 006 adds the
-- smallint sibling column; ScyllaMigrationService.BackfillPrimaryFrontAsync then copies
-- every non-null int value into the smallint column (ledger-guarded per keyspace);
-- migration 007 drops the legacy int column. That whole sequence happens inside a
-- single StartingAsync pass so the "dual-write / dual-read window" never actually
-- exists in production — the repositories switched to single-write / single-read
-- against the smallint column in the same PR that introduced these migrations.
--
-- Idempotence: the ledger row skips re-application after a successful first run.
-- If a boot crashes between the ALTER landing and the ledger row being written, the
-- next boot's ADD would surface an "Invalid column name / already exists" error;
-- ScyllaMigrationService.ExecuteStatementsStatic catches that alongside the
-- symmetric column-not-found handler used for the DROP side. Not using
-- `ADD IF NOT EXISTS` because the ScyllaDB version we target rejects the syntax
-- at parse time.
-- =====================

ALTER TABLE {{KEYSPACE}}.users ADD primary_front_smallint smallint;
